#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Modern UI Revamp PR-D - Worker 1: app shell, dashboard, list pages, sales
pipeline (issue #395 - fidelity pass).

User directive: "I want the screen and ui to be exactly same as the artifact."
This is a STRUCTURAL rebuild of Worker 1's region onto the concept artifact's
markup (.app-shell/.sidebar/.topbar/.page, .page-heading, .kpi-grid/.kpi-card,
.dash-grid, .pipeline-list/.pipeline-row, .task-list, .list-toolbar,
table.company-table, .pagination); behavior, routes, data expressions, handler
ids, data-* attributes and onclick wiring are unchanged.

app.js: exact ordinal string anchors below; every replacement asserts its
anchor matches EXACTLY once and fails loudly otherwise. No regex replaces.
styles.css: APPEND ONLY - one marker block at the end with token-mapped
artifact CSS (artifact hsl(var(--X)) -> var(--X); hsl(var(--X) / A) ->
color-mix(in srgb, var(--X) A%, transparent)); existing CSS untouched.

Deliberate deviations from the artifact (behavior preservation):
- KPI tiles stay <button> with data-kpi-nav/data-kpi-filter (they navigate);
  "+ New" quick-create menu kept on the dashboard instead of the artifact's
  "View reports" button; onboarding banner kept.
- Sidebar collapse keeps toggling .collapsed on #appSidebar (existing
  behavior incl. localStorage); the grid track shrinks via
  .app-shell:has(> .sidebar.collapsed).
- Mobile drawer keeps the .open-on-aside + hidden-on-backdrop mechanism;
  class renamed to artifact's .side-backdrop (backdrop CSS re-added).
- themeAssetsApply() needs .side-brand/.brand-mark hooks, so the product
  mark carries dual classes (side-top side-brand, mark brand-mark).
- Pipeline page keeps the app's kanban (no kanban in the artifact); deal
  cards keep Edit/Delete (data-edit/data-del) instead of the artifact's
  single overflow button. No drag behavior existed on deals - nothing kept.
- List rows keep Edit/Delete buttons; breadcrumbs kept only for filtered
  views; saved-view bar / bulk bar / grouping / bulk checkboxes untouched.
- The sidebar's version-meta/.side-bottom block was dropped per the
  artifact (website/compare/roadmap/releases links remain in Help).
- toggleSidebarCollapse() rewrites the collapse button's textContent on
  toggle (existing behavior), so the "Collapse sidebar" label shows until
  the first collapse cycle.
- Mobile (<=768px) floating pill bottom nav (#bottomNav, 5 data-nav
  buttons: Assistant / Companies / Reports / Tasks / Dashboard) - per the
  user's target screenshot; not in the static artifact markup. The
  existing renderSidebarNav()/renderView() [data-nav] wiring navigates,
  sets .active and closes the drawer automatically; CSS shows it only
  <=768px, fully token-driven.
- Dashboard keeps the "+ New" quick-create menu AND gains the artifact's
  "View reports" outline button (data-nav2="reports", picked up by
  dashboard()'s existing [data-nav2] wiring).

Usage: run from the repo root. The workflow must stage both files
(`git add app.js styles.css`) for the changes to be committed.
"""
